      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When encountering skin irregularities with atypical morphology, it's essential to select codes that describe the precise characteristics of the lesion. The ICD-10 hierarchy recommends starting with codes that list the most general conditions, then moving to more specific ones. For instance, the superficial and deep benign lesiones can be considered under L90.3. When in doubt, referring to a dermatology textbook or online resources can help.",
      "source": "target",
